<!--meta {"lead": "A breadcrumb shows where a detail page sits and gives one tap back to its parent: Styles › Knotless braids, Braiders › Nia Okafor, Appointments › HP-1048.", "description": "Path to the current page with the current item marked; collapses to the parent link on phones.", "pills": ["<code>&lt;nav&gt;</code> + <code>&lt;ol&gt;</code>", "Status: core set, recommended for detail pages"], "variants": "full path, collapsed to parent (phones)", "states": "default, hover, focus, active, current", "sources": ["pages/style-detail/default", "pages/braider-profile/default", "pages/appointment-detail/default", "pages/matching-braiders/default"]} -->
<section class="ds-section" id="overview"><h2><a href="#overview">Overview</a></h2>
  <p>Use a breadcrumb at the top of a detail page, above the <a href="page-header.html">page header</a>, when the page has a clear parent the customer may want to return to: Knotless braids, Nia's profile, appointment HP-1048 and the braiders for a style. Without it the only way back is the browser button or the top bar.</p>
  <ul>
    <li>Use it only for hierarchy (Styles › Knotless braids), not for the history of how someone arrived.</li>
    <li>Skip it on top-level pages (Styles, Braiders, Appointments, Help) and on auth and error pages.</li>
    <li>The last item is the current page, unlinked and marked with <code>aria-current="page"</code>.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="anatomy"><h2><a href="#anatomy">Anatomy</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-anatomy">
    <figure class="ds-anatomy__figure">
      <nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb, anatomy example"><ol><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html">Styles</a></li><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/style-detail/default.html">Knotless braids</a></li><li><span aria-current="page">Braiders</span></li></ol></nav>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 22%; top: 24%;" aria-hidden="true">1</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 37%; top: 24%;" aria-hidden="true">2</span>
      <span class="ds-callout" style="left: 70%; top: 24%;" aria-hidden="true">3</span>
    </figure>
    <ol class="ds-anatomy__list">
      <li><div><b>Ancestor link</b><small><code>--color-fg-muted</code>, underline on hover, 24px tall target.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Separator</b><small>"/" drawn by CSS in <code>--color-fg-subtle</code>; hidden from assistive technology.</small></div></li>
      <li><div><b>Current page</b><small>Plain text, <code>--color-fg-default</code>, medium weight, <code>aria-current="page"</code>.</small></div></li>
    </ol>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="variants"><h2><a href="#variants">Variants</a></h2>
  {{example:[stack]Full path from 768px: every ancestor, then the current page.}}
<nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb, appointment example"><ol><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/my-appointments/default.html">Appointments</a></li><li><span aria-current="page">HP-1048</span></li></ol></nav>
