  {{/example}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sizes" data-na="The breadcrumb has one size: --text-body-sm with 24px link targets."><h2><a href="#sizes">Sizes</a></h2></section>

<section class="ds-section" id="states"><h2><a href="#states">States</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-matrix"><table>
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Item</th><th scope="col">Default</th><th scope="col">Hover</th><th scope="col">Focus</th><th scope="col">Active</th><th scope="col">Current</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><th scope="row">Ancestor</th>
        <td><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="State default"><ol><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html">Styles</a></li></ol></nav></td>
        <td><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="State hover"><ol><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html" data-state="hover">Styles</a></li></ol></nav></td>
        <td><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="State focus"><ol><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html" data-state="focus">Styles</a></li></ol></nav></td>
        <td><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="State active"><ol><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html" data-state="hover">Styles</a></li></ol></nav></td>
        <td><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="State current"><ol><li><span aria-current="page">Knotless braids</span></li></ol></nav></td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
  <p>The current item is not a link, so it has no hover or focus state; the pointer-down state keeps the hover look. Breadcrumb links are never disabled.</p>
  <h3>Both themes</h3>
  {{themes}}<nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb, themes example"><ol><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html">Styles</a></li><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/style-detail/default.html" data-state="hover">Knotless braids</a></li><li><span aria-current="page">Braiders</span></li></ol></nav>{{/themes}}
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="responsive"><h2><a href="#responsive">Responsive behaviour</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li><b>Below 768px</b>: only the parent shows, with a leading chevron-left icon ("‹ Knotless braids"). It stays inside <code>&lt;nav aria-label="Breadcrumb"&gt;</code>; the current page is already the <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code>. The full path is always rendered: the stylesheet hides the other items (<code>display: none</code>, so they leave the accessibility tree) and the parent's separator.</li>
    <li><b>From 768px</b>: the full path shows and the chevron is hidden. Long paths wrap onto a second line rather than truncating.</li>
    <li>The chevron is rendered on the parent link only (the last ancestor), so it never sits in the middle of a path.</li>
    <li>Place it inside <code>.product-main</code> directly above the page header, aligned to the content edge.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="theming"><h2><a href="#theming">Theming</a></h2>
  <p>The breadcrumb reads <code>--color-fg-muted</code> (links), <code>--color-fg-subtle</code> (separator) and <code>--color-fg-default</code> (current and hover). In dark they become grey 350, 400 and 150 on the grey 950 canvas. It has no component tokens; theme it through the semantic tier.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="accessibility"><h2><a href="#accessibility">Accessibility</a></h2>
  <h3>Role and pattern</h3>
  <p><a href="https://www.w3.org/WAI/ARIA/apg/patterns/breadcrumb/">APG Breadcrumb</a>: <code>&lt;nav aria-label="Breadcrumb"&gt;</code> containing an ordered list; the current page carries <code>aria-current="page"</code>. Separators are CSS content with empty alternative text (<code>content: "/" / ""</code>), so they are not read.</p>
  <h3>Keyboard</h3>
  <table class="ds-table ds-keys"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Key</th><th scope="col">Action</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><kbd>Tab</kbd> / <kbd>Shift</kbd>+<kbd>Tab</kbd></td><td>Moves through the ancestor links; the current page is skipped.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><kbd>Enter</kbd></td><td>Follows the link.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
  <h3>Focus</h3>
  <p>The shared 2px ring with 2px offset around each link.</p>
  <h3>Labelling</h3>
  <p>The landmark is labelled "Breadcrumb" (one breadcrumb per page). Link text is the destination page's topic ("Nia Okafor", not "Nia’s profile page").</p>
  <h3>Contrast</h3>
  <div class="ds-example__canvas ds-example__canvas--stack" style="padding: 0; gap: var(--space-2);">
    {{pair:Ancestor link on page|--color-fg-muted|--color-bg-canvas|4.5}}
    {{pair:Separator on page|--color-fg-subtle|--color-bg-canvas|4.5}}
    {{pair:Current page|--color-fg-default|--color-bg-canvas|4.5}}
    {{pair:Focus ring|--color-focus-ring|--color-bg-canvas|3}}
  </div>
  <h3>Motion</h3>
  <p>None; underline and colour change instantly.</p>
  <h3>Touch</h3>
  <p>Links are at least 24px tall (<code>--target-min</code>) with 8px between items. On phones the single parent link sits alone, well clear of the page header.</p>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="content"><h2><a href="#content">Content</a></h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Each item is the short name of its page in sentence case: "Styles", "Knotless braids", "Nia Okafor", "HP-1048".</li>
    <li>Do not add "Home"; Styles is HairPop's home.</li>
    <li>The last item matches the page's <code>&lt;h1&gt;</code> topic.</li>
  </ul>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="do-dont"><h2><a href="#do-dont">Do and don't</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-dodont">
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb, do example"><ol><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/matching-braiders/default.html">Braiders</a></li><li><span aria-current="page">Nia Okafor</span></li></ol></nav></div><figcaption>Give detail pages a path back to their parent list.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><p class="text-muted">Nia Okafor (no way back but the browser)</p></div><figcaption>Leave Nia's profile, Knotless braids and appointment HP-1048 without a breadcrumb, as the first mocks did.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-do"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb, do example two"><ol><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html">Styles</a></li><li><span aria-current="page">Knotless braids</span></li></ol></nav></div><figcaption>Leave the current page as plain text.</figcaption></figure>
    <figure class="ds-dont"><div class="ds-example__canvas"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb, don't example two"><ol><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/style-gallery/default.html">Styles</a></li><li><a href="../../mocks/pages/style-detail/default.html">Knotless braids</a></li></ol></nav></div><figcaption>Link the current page to itself.</figcaption></figure>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="tokens"><h2><a href="#tokens">Tokens</a></h2>
  <div class="ds-table-wrap"><table class="ds-table">
    <thead><tr><th scope="col">Part</th><th scope="col">Token</th><th scope="col">Light</th><th scope="col">Dark</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      {{tok:Ancestor link|--color-fg-muted}}
      {{tok:Separator|--color-fg-subtle}}
      {{tok:Current, hover|--color-fg-default}}
      {{tok:Font|--text-body-sm}}
      {{tok:Current weight|--font-weight-medium}}
      {{tok:Gap|--space-2}}
      {{tok:Link target|--target-min}}
    </tbody>
  </table></div>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="code"><h2><a href="#code">Code</a></h2>
  <pre><code>&lt;nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"&gt;
  &lt;ol&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="/"&gt;Styles&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;a href="/styles/knotless-braids"&gt;&lt;svg class="icon icon--sm" aria-hidden="true" …&gt;…chevron-left…&lt;/svg&gt;Knotless braids&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
    &lt;li&gt;&lt;span aria-current="page"&gt;Braiders&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/li&gt;
  &lt;/ol&gt;
&lt;/nav&gt;</code></pre>
  <table class="ds-table"><thead><tr><th scope="col">Class / attribute</th><th scope="col">Effect</th></tr></thead><tbody>
    <tr><td><code>.breadcrumb</code> on <code>&lt;nav&gt;</code> (or the <code>&lt;ol&gt;</code>)</td><td>Wrapping row of items with CSS separators.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>aria-current="page"</code></td><td>Current page: default colour, medium weight.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>.icon.icon--sm</code> in the parent link</td><td>Back chevron; shown below 768px only.</td></tr>
    <tr><td>(viewport below 768px)</td><td>Every item but the parent is hidden, and the parent's separator; one-item lists are left alone.</td></tr>
    <tr><td><code>data-state="hover|focus"</code></td><td>Documentation only.</td></tr>
  </tbody></table>
</section>

<section class="ds-section" id="sources"><h2><a href="#sources">Sources</a></h2>
  <p>Core set, on the detail pages:</p>
  <ul>
    {{mock:pages/style-detail/default|Styles › Knotless braids}}
    {{mock:pages/braider-profile/default|Braiders › Nia Okafor}}
    {{mock:pages/appointment-detail/default|Appointments › HP-1048}}
    {{mock:pages/matching-braiders/default|Styles › Knotless braids › Braiders}}
  </ul>
  <p>Drift fixed during extraction: detail pages had no path back to their parent list (system adds a breadcrumb, now in the mocks); the starter kit's separator was read aloud by screen readers (now CSS content with empty alternative text). Added since: the collapse to the parent below 768px is a <code>components.css</code> rule, not a second markup.</p>
</section>
